<!-- WHAT'S IN THE BOX -->
<section class="what section" id="what">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="what-layout">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="tag">what's in the box</span>
        <h2 class="section-h2">Pre-sales to closed, one loop.</h2>
        <p class="what-desc">Not a scraped lead list. The studio finds the companies worth your time, proves who they are, enriches the people, writes what you'd actually send — then preps the call and remembers what worked.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="what-grid reveal d1">
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">01</div><h3>Deal discovery</h3><p>Type a company, paste a list of a hundred, or press "find more" on an empty box. The studio suggests lookalikes worth pitching and scores every one against what you told it to hunt.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">02</div><h3>Research that shows its work</h3><p>It reads the target's own website before anything else runs. Every pitch lists the pages it opened and the same-named companies it ruled out.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">03</div><h3>AI-powered enrichment</h3><p>Decision-makers named only where a credible source backs the name — rated confirmed, likely or unverified, with 1st/2nd/3rd-degree LinkedIn search chips on every row. No source, no name.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">04</div><h3>The pitch, drafted</h3><p>Pitch deck, one-pager, cold-email sequence and written proposal — on your brand, in your voice, every block editable in place, print-to-PDF over your own stylesheet.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">05</div><h3>Calls, prepped both ways</h3><p>Before a call you booked: one sheet — the goal, grounded talking points, the objection they'll raise with an answer you can say verbatim. For a call someone's asking for: paste their outreach and get take-it-or-skip-it, argued from your own brief.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">06</div><h3>Warm paths in</h3><p>Bring your network — a LinkedIn export or a pasted list — and every pitch maps you → connector → target, with a forwardable intro request drafted in your voice. No connector is ever invented.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
<section class="how section" id="how">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="how-layout">
      <div>
        <span class="tag reveal">how it works</span>
        <h2 class="section-h2 reveal">From your URL<br>to your first pitch.</h2>
        <div class="how-steps">
          <div class="how-step reveal"><span class="step-n">01</span><div><h3>Scan your site</h3><p>The field up top. The studio reads your website and proposes what it should hunt for you — that proposal is yours to confirm or sharpen.</p></div></div>
          <div class="how-step reveal d1"><span class="step-n">02</span><div><h3>Check out</h3><p>The moment payment lands, your workspace is created and researched — the studio is reading your site while you're still on the receipt page.</p></div></div>
          <div class="how-step reveal d2"><span class="step-n">03</span><div><h3>Sign in and go</h3><p>You arrive in a studio already full of you: brief drafted, goal pre-filled, three researched prospects ready to run. Use your work email and your whole team gets in.</p></div></div>
          <div class="how-step reveal d3"><span class="step-n">04</span><div><h3>Run pitches</h3><p>Thumbs-up a prospect — or paste a whole list and run it as a batch. Minutes later the research, deliverables and decision-makers are there. Your edits teach it your voice for next time.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

